Z||000000||Voyd||04-01-2000||12:30 AM||||hey,<P>i am about halfway into my restoration of a 85Se into an 85GT and today i replaced the rear bumeper. <P>well everything went well and its on now, but i didnt even notice i had forgotten to attach the little metal plates that go right above the exhaust. im guessing they are a heat sheild. my question is, does it really matter if i dont use them. or will the heat cause problems?||||reg||4
Z||000001||Oreif||04-01-2000||12:40 AM||||If the car is going to be a daily driver and you sit in a lot of traffic it will warp the plastic a bit. The plates are also protection if the exhaust pipe gets loose and the hot pipe comes in contact it will melt the plastic.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Voyd||04-04-2000||11:37 PM||||anyone else? this bumper is a prime condition and i dont want to screw it up, yet i dont really wanna take it off again.||||reg||1
Z||000003||WKDFIRO||04-04-2000||11:53 PM||||I didn't think of it till now but I put a Formula rear end on my 85 GT and there doesn't seem to be any problem with the urethane. There are no plates there. Now keep in mind that it is black so I don't know what it would do to a different color paint but I have not seen or noticed any problems.||||reg||2
